# Page Size and Optimization Rule

- Keep every `page` file at or below 300 lines.
- If a page grows beyond 300 lines, extract UI sections into route-local components (for example `app/<route>/_components/*`).
- Move reusable logic into shared hooks/utilities only when it is used across multiple routes.
- Prefer small, focused components with clear props to reduce re-render surface area.
- Keep generated code optimization-first: avoid unnecessary state, expensive computations in render, and duplicate data fetching.
- Use memoization (`useMemo`, `useCallback`, `React.memo`) only when there is a measurable or obvious render-performance benefit.
